The same topic pops up every now and then.
But you see, nethack is not a kind of game that would work very well
as a multi-user game.. You know, you may take as long as you want to
figure out what to do with your move, where you move or do you want to
do something else like read a scroll or quaff a potion, or save the
game and come back later.

If there were more users, the others would have to wait *an undefined time*
until you decide what you do. Or, if there was a time limet, the slower
players, who like to think it over thoroughly, would be forced to the 
faster rhythm or the more reckless players would always hack them in
pieces. And what about when somebody wants to save and the others want
to go on..

Either way, the game wouldn't be the same anymore.
